# PowerShell coverage exclusions for the xp-gate pre-commit hook.
#
# One glob per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Matched source files are removed from Pester's -CodeCoverage path list.
#
# The list is intentionally EMPTY.
# -------------------------------
# It used to hold exactly one file, setup.ps1, on the grounds that its `Main`
# ended in `exit 0` / `exit 1` and therefore killed the Pester host when
# dot-sourced, making it "structurally unmeasurable". That was a code defect
# dressed up as a structural limit: ADR-001 moved the exit code to
# `[ref]$ExitCode` and put `exit` only in the execution guard, so setup.ps1 is
# now instrumented like every other script (tests/unit/scripts.Tests.ps1 calls
# its Main in-process).
#
# Do NOT add files here merely because they are hard to test. If a script really
# cannot be instrumented, prove it in the commit message and fix the script first.
